WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.170
Every MyWell user can read every station's
data, not just their own.

2
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:09.898
This tutorial is about how to get at it: pick
an area on the map,

3
00:00:10.018 --> 00:00:13.018
then look at its trend and its statistics.

4
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.730
Now we're on: Monitoring area.

5
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.514
This map covers the whole community.

6
00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:24.914
A Monitoring Area is a saved group of stations
you pick once and re-open anytime —

7
00:00:25.034 --> 00:00:28.298
the controls here let you build and explore
them.

8
00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:31.229
Open a monitoring area.

9
00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:35.357
A monitoring area is a saved set of stations
you follow together.

10
00:00:35.477 --> 00:00:41.741
We've opened the sample ‘Badgaon village’ area for
you — see the map focus on just its stations.

11
00:00:41.861 --> 00:00:45.221
Pick any area here to scope the whole page to
it.

12
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.826
Filter by type.

13
00:00:47.946 --> 00:00:55.050
Open Station type to show or hide each kind of
station — groundwater wells, rainfall, check-dams,

14
00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.946
rivers and more.

15
00:00:57.066 --> 00:00:59.418
It doubles as the map legend.

16
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.530
Find specific stations.

17
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:08.746
Use Station to search by name or code and pick just
the stations you want; the map narrows to them.

18
00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.326
Build an area.

19
00:01:11.446 --> 00:01:17.494
Actions is how you create an area: Pick
stations one by one, Draw an area on the map,

20
00:01:17.614 --> 00:01:20.494
or Select area by dragging a box.

21
00:01:20.614 --> 00:01:23.902
Save it and it appears in My Monitoring Areas.

22
00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.541
Now see its data.

23
00:01:26.661 --> 00:01:30.069
Once an area is picked, this card appears.

24
00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:36.381
Open Data trend for its readings charted over time,
or Data statistics for a ranked breakdown.

25
00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:39.765
Your own saved areas open the same way.

26
00:01:40.583 --> 00:01:43.271
Now we're on: Data trend.

27
00:01:43.391 --> 00:01:47.879
This page charts how readings change over time
across a whole area.

28
00:01:47.999 --> 00:01:52.895
It opens empty on purpose — you begin by
choosing a Monitoring Area.

29
00:01:53.717 --> 00:01:55.733
Your monitoring areas.

30
00:01:55.853 --> 00:01:59.069
A monitoring area is a saved set of stations.

31
00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:04.709
Open My Monitoring Areas to switch between
“All stations” and any area you've saved,

32
00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:07.205
or the built-in Example area.

33
00:02:08.017 --> 00:02:10.345
One line, over time.

34
00:02:10.465 --> 00:02:16.993
Once an area is chosen, Data trend draws its
readings as a line, bar or area chart —

35
00:02:17.113 --> 00:02:19.801
the shape of the water through the seasons.

36
00:02:19.921 --> 00:02:22.753
Narrow it further with the filters above.

37
00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:25.359
Read the chart.

38
00:02:25.479 --> 00:02:29.343
Below the map, this panel charts the stations
in view.

39
00:02:29.463 --> 00:02:36.711
Pick a measurement type, time range and chart
style (Line, Bar or Area) to explore the data.

40
00:02:37.517 --> 00:02:40.493
Now we're on: Data statistics.

41
00:02:40.613 --> 00:02:47.261
The same data as Data trend, shown as numbers
instead of a line: a per-station table of averages,

42
00:02:47.381 --> 00:02:50.861
highs and lows, with the map shaded to match.

43
00:02:51.683 --> 00:02:53.699
Your monitoring areas.

44
00:02:53.819 --> 00:02:57.035
A monitoring area is a saved set of stations.

45
00:02:57.155 --> 00:03:02.675
Open My Monitoring Areas to switch between
“All stations” and any area you've saved,

46
00:03:02.795 --> 00:03:05.171
or the built-in Example area.

47
00:03:05.983 --> 00:03:08.071
The numbers, ranked.

48
00:03:08.191 --> 00:03:15.655
Data statistics answers 'which stations, and how
much?' — a sortable table of each station's average,

49
00:03:15.775 --> 00:03:19.831
highest and lowest values, with the map shaded
to match.

50
00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.426
Read the chart.

51
00:03:22.546 --> 00:03:26.410
Below the map, this panel charts the stations
in view.

52
00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:33.778
Pick a measurement type, time range and chart
style (Line, Bar or Area) to explore the data.

53
00:03:34.583 --> 00:03:36.527
That is the whole page.

54
00:03:36.647 --> 00:03:41.303
You can replay this tutorial any time from the
Learning page inside the app.

55
00:03:41.423 --> 00:03:44.399
Thanks for helping look after our groundwater.
